{
 "manufacturer": "Janitza",
 "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
 "model": "UMG 104 power analyser (RS-485 Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "umg-104",
 "short_model": "UMG 104",
 "aliases": [
  "UMG104",
  "UMG 104",
  "Janitza UMG104"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Power meter (power analyser)",
 "applies_to": "UMG 104 DIN-rail power analyser, firmware 1.268, per address list 1.041.006.1.e (01/2023).",
 "summary": "The UMG 104 is a power analyser with four voltage and four current inputs and RS-485 / RS-232 serial ports, acting as a Modbus slave. Values are big-endian 32-bit floats that already include the CT/VT ratios. This map covers the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block, the fourth channel, consumed/delivered energy totals, digital I/O, the RS-485 address and energy reset commands.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 2,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "Addresses are printed as the protocol address and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The list starts at address 0 (real-time clock), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": "1.268",
 "source": {
  "title": "Power Analyser UMG 104 - Modbus-address list and Formulary (Firmware 1.268)",
  "doc_number": "1.041.006.1.e",
  "revision_date": "2023-01",
  "url": "https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG104/janitza-mal-umg104-en.pdf",
  "pages": "Functions p. 4; transfer parameters, byte order, number formats p. 5; frequently required readings p. 12; date/time p. 13; measured values pp. 14-15; other values pp. 25-27; energy pp. 28-31"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Byte order: the list says its addresses return data big-endian (high byte first, high word in the lower register = ABCD). Adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian; that mirror block is not listed.",
  "Data types in the list: short = signed 16-bit, int = signed 32-bit, uint = unsigned 32-bit, float = IEEE 754 32-bit. Float and integer values include the CT/VT ratios; short values do not.",
  "19068 in the frequently-read block is the consumed energy of tariff 1 (rate 1) only, so it is left out; the all-tariff consumed and delivered totals are taken from the energy table (9851 / 9863).",
  "Transfer parameters (p. 5): 9600-115200 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, the UMG 104 sends 2 stop bits. The list does not give a default baud rate or device address.",
  "Left out: RS-485 mode and baud rate (10182 / 10184), RS-232 settings and IP settings, because the list gives no value coding for them; the summed power factor at 1373, whose formula is printed as Psum3/Qsum3 (likely a typo); the SHORT copies of values; harmonics, min/max/mean blocks, monthly energy, tariffs 3/4 and comparators.",
  "Left out: the CT/VT ratio rows 10032-10062. They are four-element arrays and every element is labelled 'L1, L2, L3', so which element belongs to which input is not clear from the list."
 ],
